			title: "Polarised Pellet"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 9.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["57862F697D22D7F2"]
			description: ["The &6Mk5 Fusion Ring&r has an octagon of casing round an empty channel, lined with metallic hydrogen coils. It holds a very large buffer and takes sixteen hatches. A UIV hull, UIV components, optical mainframes, the Mk5 fusion casing, metallic hydrogen coil blocks and sixteen UIV energy hatches. The three polarised burns, and the direct energy converter that turns plasma into power. Build the fuel plant before you light the ring; helium-3 and protons return to their lines."]
			icon: "gtceu:uiv_fusion_reactor"
			id: "72D797E3DDE7ED0E"
			rewards: [{ id: "1FC1422722F775DB", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "1A652572858A4F0D", item: "gtceu:uiv_fusion_reactor", type: "item" }
				{ id: "53473C5B47FD0440", item: "grindless:uiv_fusion_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7CDEE0EEBF355CAF", item: "grindless:metallic_hydrogen_coil_block", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Mk5 Fusion Ring"
			x: 4.5d
			y: 8.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B955176F4E8579C"]
			description: ["A computer built in shells, in nine times Earth's sunlight, running logic that makes barely any heat. The &6Matrioshka Computer&r is where UIV research is written. A UIV hull, UIV components, optical mainframes and the UIV casing, in Mercury orbit. Verified writes, the Kerr and equation of state charts, and the radiators that carry its heat. Logic tiles are among the longest builds here: stock them by ME and send the waste heat to the radiators."]
			icon: "gtceu:matrioshka_computer"
			id: "7E2EF99503F9DB02"
			rewards: [{ id: "79DC492E9F485905", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "3FA8AB714439F04F", item: "gtceu:matrioshka_computer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5268F067E9039C63", item: "gtceu:uiv_machine_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Matrioshka Computer"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 11.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E2EF99503F9DB02"]
			description: ["Heat has nowhere to go in space but out. Liquid tin droplets falling in free fall carry it away, which only works in orbit. The &6Droplet Radiator Works&r builds the modules. A UIV hull, UIV components and the UIV casing; the modules are assembled in Mercury orbit. Radiator modules, and the TPV tiles of the Matrioshka shell. Tin overflow returns to stock; ship modules down by ME."]
			icon: "gtceu:droplet_radiator_works"
			id: "582C5EF34B1CF2D0"
			rewards: [{ id: "1DCB16BA2FB047FA", type: "xp", xp: 200 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "383AB123F0016727", item: "gtceu:droplet_radiator_works", type: "item" }
				{ id: "31AE930D6D7F4E0A", item: "gtceu:uiv_machine_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Droplet Radiators"
			x: 4.5d
			y: 11.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["582C5EF34B1CF2D0"]
			description: ["A module of droplet radiator. The UIV Lines chart shows what it cools."]
			icon: "grindless:droplet_radiator_module"
			id: "5D28F8D529A7274F"
			rewards: [{ id: "56D6AD6ED8D998F9", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "100E346DEF63A00F", item: "grindless:droplet_radiator_module", type: "item" }]
			title: "Radiator Module"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 11.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1A781FD07AF49721"]
			description: ["A tether down to the poles and the star's own electric field carry a little of the crust up. The &6Crust Lift&r is fiction: no tether survives that gravity, and the yield is a game number. A UIV hull, the UIV casing and the neutron star site casing, with a winch. Crust matter, which the drip separator takes apart. Nothing here is voided: crust ions and nuclei go to their own tanks."]
			icon: "gtceu:crust_lift"
			id: "3DF069B74A45CB2C"
			rewards: [{ id: "5504CF031F7F42F0", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "750DDD0127C441C3", item: "gtceu:crust_lift", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1D24057E59E72584", item: "gtceu:uiv_machine_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "320D8123FCD97E70", item: "grindless:neutron_star_site_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Crust Lift"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 15.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3DF069B74A45CB2C"]
			description: ["A slab of crust, lifted from a star that has no ground. Everything taken from it is contained."]
			icon: "grindless:neutron_star_crust"
			id: "72374D6E027767FB"
			rewards: [{ id: "5B00A8545B0D00AF", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "3CB6269E59ABF867", item: "grindless:neutron_star_crust", type: "item" }]
			title: "Neutron Star Crust"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 13.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3DF069B74A45CB2C"]
			description: ["Deep in the crust the nuclei are so crowded that neutrons leak out between them. The &6Neutron Drip Separator&r takes them away before the matter relaxes. A UIV hull, the UIV casing and the neutron star site casing. Drip neutrons, for the cage and for the r-process. Drip neutrons decay if you wait, so pipe them straight to the next machine."]
			icon: "gtceu:neutron_drip_separator"
			id: "3B397C1EFE90548C"
			rewards: [{ id: "7155E482279A087A", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5C23A1C234D96D2D", item: "gtceu:neutron_drip_separator", type: "item" }
				{ id: "70C3DDD8049E55E8", item: "gtceu:uiv_machine_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "37C5FAF6AC405C0C", item: "grindless:neutron_star_site_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Neutron Drip Separator"
			x: 4.5d
			y: 15.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3B397C1EFE90548C"]
			description: ["A bucket of free neutrons that will not wait. Use it the moment it arrives."]
			icon: "gtceu:drip_neutrons_bucket"
			id: "17BF788859530203"
			rewards: [{ id: "39FDB6363E92065B", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "53DBA67730407384", item: "gtceu:drip_neutrons_bucket", type: "item" }]
			title: "Drip Neutrons"
			x: 4.5d
			y: 13.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3B397C1EFE90548C"]
			description: ["Cool the drip neutrons into a superfluid and shut it in a cage. The &6Neutronium Cage&r makes the pellet, which is fiction: a spoonful of neutron matter held at ordinary pressure by a field. A UIV hull, the UIV casing, the neutron star site casing and a coil cage. The neutronium pellet, which the gate store asks for and the compression hall reads. Drip neutrons by pipe; keep pellets by ME, as the hall never uses them up."]
			icon: "gtceu:neutronium_cage"
			id: "7B6BAE4236338966"
			rewards: [{ id: "5116545605605FDD", type: "xp", xp: 300 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "76533E1207F2D473", item: "gtceu:neutronium_cage", type: "item" }
				{ id: "50AED0A2DD0E93D5", item: "gtceu:uiv_machine_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "76FD2A4573C38B5B", item: "grindless:neutron_star_site_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Neutronium Cage"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 15.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B6BAE4236338966"]
			description: ["It is not the neutronium of the other mods: it is a pellet of neutron matter. Keep one for the hall and one for the gate."]
			icon: "grindless:neutronium_pellet"
			id: "39FBA237010D5C97"
			rewards: [{ id: "548ECF5E1DB1674F", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
